"""
Guide Corpus Decomposer  (PART-2 next stage: "LLM Smart Extraction Pipeline")

Reads the scraped guide corpus produced by guide_extractor.py
(d:\\new_automation\\app_guides_master.xlsx, sheet "App_Guides") and turns the
free-text manual Markdown into structured Action-State Trajectory JSON.

Design laws (matching the Hojaiga product laws):
  * The JSON is GENERATED BY THE MODEL, never hard-coded here. This script only
    loads guides, builds a strict prompt, calls the local model and stores the
    returned JSON. No {ui_target, expected_state_change} template lives in code.
  * App-level 70/30 split. An app appears in exactly one half (TRAIN or EVAL) so
    the eval set measures true zero-shot generalisation, not memorised UI.
  * Honest reporting. Every guide gets an explicit status (generated / no-json /
    model-down / empty). Nothing is faked as a pass; failures are logged, never
    swallowed.
  * Pilot first. By default only a small, deliberately diverse batch of complex
    apps is decomposed. Unleash the full corpus with --full once the pilot is
    flawless.
  * Fully offline w.r.t. the desktop. This stage touches no window and no cursor;
    it never disturbs the minimized-app / virtual-mouse runtime.

Local models (all resident, no keys, no cloud):
  * eyes / reasoning default : Qwen3-VL-8B via llama.cpp  (http://127.0.0.1:8081)
  * fallback text model      : Ollama                     (http://127.0.0.1:11434)

Usage
-----
  python decompose_guides.py                          # assign split + run pilot (5 apps)
  python decompose_guides.py --pilot 10               # bigger pilot batch
  python decompose_guides.py --apps "Word,Blender"    # explicit apps
  python decompose_guides.py --full                   # the whole corpus (slow)
  python decompose_guides.py --assign-split           # just write split manifest + Excel col
  python decompose_guides.py --write-excel-split      # add Dataset_Split column to the xlsx
"""

